import{_ as t,o as i,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 237 | Realm and Economy: The Realm Foundation of More-Work-More-Reward Distribution","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 237 | Realm and Economy: The Realm Foundation of More-Work-More-Reward Distribution","no":237,"module":1,"tags":["Realm","Economy","More Work More Reward","Distribution"],"related":["06-More Work More Reward Distribution Principle","22-Resource Allocation Joint Contracting Mechanism","41-Symbiotic Labor Law"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0237_模块1-境界与经济-多劳多得分配的境界基础.md","filePath":"en/0237_模块1-境界与经济-多劳多得分配的境界基础.md"}'),r={name:"en/0237_模块1-境界与经济-多劳多得分配的境界基础.md"};function a(s,e,l,u,c,d){return i(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-237-realm-and-economy-the-realm-foundation-of-more-work-more-reward-distribution" tabindex="-1">Entry 237 | Realm and Economy: The Realm Foundation of More-Work-More-Reward Distribution <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-237-realm-and-economy-the-realm-foundation-of-more-work-more-reward-distribution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 237 | Realm and Economy: The Realm Foundation of More-Work-More-Reward Distribution&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 1 · In-Depth Realm Refinement | Baseline references: Documents 06, 22, 41</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-cultivation-is-labor-contribution-is-reward" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Cultivation is labor, contribution is reward <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-cultivation-is-labor-contribution-is-reward" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Cultivation is labor, contribution is reward&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou (Wanling Hengmao Origin Cosmos)&#39;s economic system&#39;s core principle is more work more reward. And &quot;work&quot; measurement is closely tied to realm — not &quot;the higher the realm the more the reward,&quot; but <strong>the higher the realm, the greater the contribution one can make, the more reward for contribution</strong>. Realm is &quot;labor ability&quot; foundation, contribution is &quot;labor&quot; content, reward is &quot;labor&quot; result. The three are tightly linked through the Joint Contracting mechanism.</p><p>The six top-level axioms are directly embodied in the relationship between realm and economy: the anti-predation axiom negates getting something for nothing; the republican axiom of Myriad Races ensures fair distribution; the collective ascension axiom guides economy to serve civilization ascension; the causal self-discipline axiom constrains economic behavior not to damage ecology; the law-first axiom ensures distribution laws are stable and self-consistent; the universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><p>This entry analyzes how the more-work-more-reward distribution system operates based on realm.</p><h2 id="i-the-relationship-between-realm-and-contribution-output" tabindex="-1">I. The Relationship Between Realm and Contribution Output <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-the-relationship-between-realm-and-contribution-output" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. The Relationship Between Realm and Contribution Output&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Realm</th><th>Typical Contribution Type</th><th>Contribution Output Magnitude</th><th>Distribution Tier</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sense - Condensed Origin</td><td>Basic service, community contribution</td><td>Personal-level</td><td>Basic allotment</td></tr><tr><td>Transform - Law Origin</td><td>Tech R&amp;D, mentor guidance</td><td>Community-level</td><td>Advanced allotment</td></tr><tr><td>Dao - Dao Integration</td><td>Law research, regional management</td><td>Regional-level</td><td>High-tier allotment</td></tr><tr><td>Boundary-Breaking - World-Creation</td><td>Plane coordination, world-creation engineering</td><td>Plane-level</td><td>Plane-level allotment</td></tr><tr><td>Origin Realm</td><td>Law fine-tuning, cosmic governance</td><td>Cosmic-level</td><td>Cosmic-level allotment</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="ii-why-realm-is-the-foundation-of-distribution" tabindex="-1">II. Why Realm Is the Foundation of Distribution <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-realm-is-the-foundation-of-distribution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why Realm Is the Foundation of Distribution&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_2-1-realm-determines-contribution-ability" tabindex="-1">2.1 Realm Determines Contribution Ability <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-1-realm-determines-contribution-ability" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.1 Realm Determines Contribution Ability&quot;">​</a></h3><p>It is not &quot;high realm gets more,&quot; but &quot;high realm can make greater contributions.&quot; One Origin Realm strong one&#39;s one law fine-tuning benefits the entire cosmos; a Sense Origin cultivator&#39;s contribution can only benefit a few around them. Differences in contribution magnitude objectively determine differences in distribution tier.</p><p>This is not &quot;distribute by realm,&quot; but &quot;distribute by contribution&quot; — it&#39;s just that high-realm cultivators can objectively make greater contributions.</p><h3 id="_2-2-realm-advancement-requires-continuous-investment" tabindex="-1">2.2 Realm Advancement Requires Continuous Investment <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-2-realm-advancement-requires-continuous-investment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.2 Realm Advancement Requires Continuous Investment&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The cultivation process from Sense Origin to Origin Realm requires continuous investment of time, energy, and resources. The more-work-more-reward principle is also embodied here — the more you invest in cultivation (the higher the realm), the greater your contribution potential to civilization, and the more returns you receive. This is reasonable return on cultivation investment.</p><h3 id="_2-3-but-realm-is-not-the-only-distribution-criterion" tabindex="-1">2.3 But Realm Is Not the Only Distribution Criterion <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-3-but-realm-is-not-the-only-distribution-criterion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.3 But Realm Is Not the Only Distribution Criterion&quot;">​</a></h3><p>More-work-more-reward is not realm-only. A Transform Origin cultivator who undertakes a large amount of mentor work and public service may have a contribution value exceeding a Dao Origin cultivator who cultivates in seclusion. The core of distribution is &quot;contribution value&quot;; realm is only one dimension of contribution ability.</p><h2 id="iii-distribution-s-concrete-mechanism" tabindex="-1">III. Distribution&#39;s Concrete Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-distribution-s-concrete-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Distribution&#39;s Concrete Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_3-1-contribution-value-auto-measurement" tabindex="-1">3.1 Contribution Value Auto-Measurement <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-1-contribution-value-auto-measurement" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.1 Contribution Value Auto-Measurement&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The anchor network auto-records all cultivator contributions:</p><ul><li>Cultivation breakthrough contributions: realm advancement, new method creation</li><li>Knowledge sharing contributions: insight upload, teaching coaching</li><li>Tech R&amp;D contributions: law engineering innovation</li><li>Public service contributions: anchor maintenance, community service</li><li>Guardianship contributions: threat defense, rescue</li></ul><p>Each contribution has a quantitative score, aggregated into personal contribution value.</p><h3 id="_3-2-joint-contracting-linkage" tabindex="-1">3.2 Joint Contracting Linkage <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-2-joint-contracting-linkage" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.2 Joint Contracting Linkage&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Contribution value directly links to resource allotment:</p><ul><li>Higher contribution value, higher resource allotment priority</li><li>Contribution value reaching different thresholds unlocks different tiers of resource permissions</li><li>Contribution value persistently low, resource allotment returns to basic level</li></ul><h3 id="_3-3-progressive-adjustment-tax" tabindex="-1">3.3 Progressive Adjustment Tax <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-3-progressive-adjustment-tax" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.3 Progressive Adjustment Tax&quot;">​</a></h3><p>High contributors pay progressive adjustment tax (up to 30%), used for the Everyone-Has-a-Road Guarantee System. This ensures distribution differences do not lead to polarization — strong ones get more, but also give back to society through tax.</p><h2 id="iv-the-dialectic-between-realm-and-economy" tabindex="-1">IV. The Dialectic Between Realm and Economy <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-the-dialectic-between-realm-and-economy" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. The Dialectic Between Realm and Economy&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Realm advancement promotes economic contribution; economic resources feed back realm advancement — this is a positive feedback loop:</p><ul><li>Cultivator realm advancement → contribution ability strengthens → contribution value rises → obtains more resources → resources feed back cultivation → realm further advances</li></ul><p>This loop&#39;s key is: <strong>contribution is the intermediate step</strong> — you cannot directly buy realm with resources; you must first make contributions to obtain resources, then use resources to cultivate and advance realm. This ensures economic resources always flow to those &quot;truly creating value.&quot;</p><h2 id="v-why-not-distribute-directly-by-realm" tabindex="-1">V. Why Not Distribute Directly by Realm <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-why-not-distribute-directly-by-realm" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Why Not Distribute Directly by Realm&quot;">​</a></h2><p>If distributing directly by realm (&quot;you are Dao Origin so you automatically get Dao Origin&#39;s resources&quot;), it would cause:</p><ul><li>Some lying flat: reaching a certain realm then no longer contributing, eating from stored grain</li><li>Resource waste: people not working occupy resources without working</li><li>Incentive failure: since realm equals reward, why work hard to contribute?</li></ul><p>So distribution&#39;s core is always &quot;contribution value&quot;; realm is only a reference dimension of contribution ability. An Origin Realm strong one who does nothing may have resource allotment lower than a Transform Origin cultivator actively contributing — this is true more work more reward.</p><h2 id="vi-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">VI. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Universal infinite backstop</strong>: the universal equal infinite law establishes that every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing have a guarantee, strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose, predation naturally loses meaning</li><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: more work more reward ensures resources flow to those most able to create value, no &quot;occupying resources without working&quot; waste</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: distribution based on contribution not violence, predators cannot obtain legitimate resources through predation</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo systems&#39; economy is &quot;strong rob weak&quot;; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s economy is &quot;more work more reward, progressive adjustment&quot;</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the distribution system is equal for every Myriad Races group, each race&#39;s contributions are measured</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: contribution measurement and distribution mechanisms expand with cosmos expansion, cross-cosmos contributions also measured</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The relationship between realm and economy is not &quot;the stronger the richer,&quot; but &quot;the stronger the more able to make greater contributions, the greater the contribution the more the reward.&quot; The more-work-more-reward distribution system takes realm as ability foundation, contribution as measurement standard, Joint Contracting as implementation mechanism, ensuring unity of efficiency and fairness. In predatory-faction systems, economy is robbed; in the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, economy is earned — this is the fundamental difference between realm and economy relationship.</p><p>In the final analysis, realm and economy · the realm foundation of more-work-more-reward distribution described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./06-多劳多得分配原理.html">06-More Work More Reward Distribution Principle</a> · <a href="./22-资源分配联产承包机制.html">22-Resource Allocation Joint Contracting Mechanism</a> · <a href="./41-共生劳动法.html">41-Symbiotic Labor Law</a></li></ul>',41)])])}const b=t(r,[["render",a]]);export{h as __pageData,b as default};
